# Data-Prep Spec: {{ dataset_name }}

**Format:** {{ format }} (chat | completion | dpo)
**Target base model:** {{ base_model }}
**Owner:** {{ owner }}
**Date:** {{ date }}

## 1. Source

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Origin | {{ source_origin }} (csv / parquet / db dump, path or query) |
| Raw row count | {{ raw_row_count }} |
| Rows dropped (empty / duplicate) | {{ dropped_row_count }} |
| Columns used | {{ columns_used }} |
| Label column (classification only) | {{ label_column }} |

## 2. Transform

### Schema map (rule r1-jsonl-schema)

| JSONL field | Source column |
|-------------|---------------|
| `messages[0]` system | canonical prompt below (constant) |
| `messages[1]` user | {{ user_column }} |
| `messages[2]` assistant | {{ assistant_column }} |
| `non_preferred_output` (dpo only) | {{ rejected_column }} |

### Canonical system prompt (rule r5-deterministic-system-prompt)

One string, identical on every line. Never varied per example.

```
<system_prompt>
```

### PII scrub (rule r6-no-pii)

| Pattern | Action | Matches found |
|---------|--------|---------------|
| email | replace with sha256 token | {{ pii_email_count }} |
| phone (E.164 / national) | replace with sha256 token | {{ pii_phone_count }} |
| customer / ticket IDs | replace with sha256 token | {{ pii_id_count }} |

`pii_scrubbed: <pii_scrubbed>` (must be `true` before upload).

### Token budget (rule r2-token-budget)

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Tokenizer | tiktoken `<tiktoken_encoding>` |
| Context cap enforced | <context_cap_tokens> tokens |
| Examples rejected over cap | {{ over_cap_count }} |
| Max tokens / example | <max_tokens_per_example> |
| Total tokens (one epoch) | {{ total_tokens }} |
| Planned epochs | {{ epochs }} |
| Training price ($ / 1M tokens) | <price_per_1m_usd> |
| **Estimated cost (USD)** | **{{ estimated_usd }}** |

## 3. Split (rule r3-train-val-split, r4-balanced-classes)

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Strategy | hash-disjoint on user text, seed `<split_seed>` |
| Ratio | {{ split_ratio }} (80/20 default; 70/30 when total < 500) |
| Train count | {{ train_count }} |
| Validation count | {{ val_count }} |
| Class ratio before / after balancing | {{ class_ratio_before }} / {{ class_ratio_after }} (cap 1.5x) |

Validation rows are never used for training and never reused as the eval held-out set.

## 4. Output

| Artifact | Value |
|----------|-------|
| `train_path` | {{ train_path }} |
| `val_path` | {{ val_path }} |
| OpenAI training file ID | {{ training_file_id }} |
| OpenAI validation file ID | {{ validation_file_id }} |
| Validator report | {{ validator_report_path }} (`openai-validate-jsonl.py` exit 0) |

## 5. Self-check

- [ ] Every line parses and carries the `<format>` schema (r1)
- [ ] No example exceeds <context_cap_tokens> tokens (r2)
- [ ] Train and validation are hash-disjoint; ratio matches the rule (r3)
- [ ] Class ratio within 1.5x or balancing recorded above (r4)
- [ ] Single canonical system prompt across all lines (r5)
- [ ] `pii_scrubbed: true` with match counts recorded (r6)
- [ ] `scripts/validate-fine-tuning-openai-data-prep.py` exits 0
